*******************************************************************************************************     The Print Manager*            LaserWriter Driver using AppleTalk** Copyright 1986-1993 Apple Computer, Inc.* All Rights Reserved******************************************************************************************************** Coding Started Summer 1986 by Luc Barthelet and VersionSoft** Version 1.0** May 07, 1987    Suki Lee** Version 1.1** Jul 02, 1987    Suki Lee**    Major rewrite of routines which deal with PAP calls for AppleTalk. New alert box*    is added to allow user to restart LaserWriter without physically turning it off*    and on.**    Fixed paper size in points in PrtRecord.Dflt for US Legal and A4 Letter.**    New call: PrPixelMap - prints given pixel map*              input: SrcLocPtr   - LONG*     	  SrcRectPtr  - LONG*                     ColorFlag   - WORD - 0 = B/W; else color*              output: none**    Status updated	each time a PAPWrite is issued. All custom QD calls now save and*    restore values on QD's zero page to ensure that they have not been trashed by*    the changing of the current port by the status update.** Version 2.0** Feb 01, 1988    Suki Lee**    Major revision	of the code to use a different PostScript dictionary than that*    use by the Macintosh. This dictionary is no longer a separate text file as*    before but rather a dynamic segment. The driver downloads the needed procedures*    with each print job. Nothing permanent remains in the printer, so there's no*    problem with version collision or running low on virtual memory.**    Added capability to print using resident LaserWriter Plus fonts.**    Implemented routines to process PicComments dealing with encapsulating PostScript.**    Bug Fixes:**     - String buffer used to hold parsed printer status string is increased from 50*       to 100 characters.*     - In text, if	drawverb is drawchar, the string length	is not checked.*     - The insertion point moves to the "From" box when the "From" button is clicked.*     - Rectangular	clip regions are now implemented as specified in ERS.*     - Reorganized	zero page to avoid collisions with QD's zero page since some*       routines are called with either zero page in effect, e.g. Color,*       AddStrToWBuff, etc.** Version 2.1** June 8, 1988    Suki Lee**    Added back capability to download bitmap fonts which has missing since V 1.0*    release.**    Added Command-F command to redirect PostScript to a file. This file is named*    'PostScript.GS' and is put in the /system/drivers directory of boot disk.**    PrPixelMap works once again.**    Bug Fixes:**     - Safeguards against pixel maps whose width is not on	a byte boundary.*     - Consistent reporting of error conditions reported from the printer, such*       as out of paper or font not found. (This was underlying cause of problem*       printing to non-plus LaserWriters.)*     - Added default values for flags in prepfile*     - Complete characters of downloaded bitmap fonts are now printed.*     - Italics flag was not defined for Courier font causing PostScript errors.*     - ZapfDingBats and Symbol fonts can now be printed.*     - Clean up PostScript stack after outline or shadow styles are made.*     - Corrected modified names used in fonts' entry into PostScript's FontDirectory*       after a style modification.*     - Findfont call was moved to the rf call to decrease the amount of PostScript*       sent with each font change. The code for handling the Shaston font has now*       modified accordingly to deal with that change.*     - Extended the procs "up" and "dn" to save global and graphics state variables*       across the save and restore.*** Version 2.2** July 27, 1988    Suki Lee**    Added filtering of user abort error returning from OpenLaser.**    Added clearing of PicComment flag in PrCloseDoc in case of an error condition*    occuring before PostScriptEnd comment is called.**    Modified the cursor handling code to use GetCursorAd to get original cursor*    and use SetCursor to restore after printing.**    Bug Fixes:**     - The source rectangle of the image was being used to set the scale of the*       image on the page, resulting in pictures not being scaled. The destination*       rectangle is now being used, as should be.*     - Added capability to handle downloaded bitmap fonts whose characters' image*       are wider than 32 bits. These include some 36 point fonts and most 48 and*       larger point fonts.*     - Modified status display code to use LETextBox2 so longer strings will be*       word wrapped. Problem was especially noticeable in 320 mode when printing*       to a spooler.*     - At start of each print job, zeros out the NewInterval variable used as the*       5 second timer for status calls. Status can be skipped if the timer is not*       zeroed each time.*     - EraseRect was printing a black rectangle instead of white. The code was*       behaving as if it were a fill. Modified to use PostScript's newpath call,*       which draws nothing. This is the same as filling with background color*       since background is white on paper.** Version 3.0 on system disk 5.0, 5.0.1, 5.0.2** d1* October 20, 1988    Suki Lee**    Eliminated some old PostScript strings that are no longer used.**    Added code in MakeBMFont to check for the case where the height of the image*    is negative (this can happen if the imagewidth is nonzero but all the bits in*    the font strike are 0) and marks it as undefined so as not to print garbage.**    Added capability to set the jobname in the LaserWriter's status dictionary so*    AppleTalk can use it to report status.**    Modified error checking after OpenFile call in DownLoadFile to pass ProDOS*    errors to application instead of TLMountVolume call.** November 11, 1988    Suki Lee**    Modified references of FontID to FontFamNum where appropriate. Also modified*    the naming of downloaded fonts to use its family name instead of its family*    number. This is the start of a move away from using font family numbers as*    identifiers for fonts.** d2* November 29, 1988    Suki Lee**    Added constant for AppleTalk's flow quantum.**    Added code to query the LaserWriter's FontDirectory and read the data into*    a buffer. Two tables, one for length of the names and one for offsets into*    the buffer, are stuffed by parsing the buffer.**    Two new calls are added: PrGetPrinterSpecs, which returns the printer's type*    and its characteristics (only color capability is defined for now) and*    PrGetPageOrientation which returns either portrait or landscape. These calls*    are needed by IIGS HyperCard printing.**    Added call to Print Manager to get document's name to provide a more complete*    status message. The message now appears as: "job: User - user name, Document*    - doc name; status: busy; source: AppleTalk." PrCloseDoc resets the name to*    the default string "Unknown", making the name valid for the duration of the*    job only.** d3* December 12, 1988    Suki Lee**    Refined the logic to search the LaserWriter's font directory for the existence*    of the current font. A table is used to look up style modifications to compose*    a full font name to be used for string matches with the directory.** December 15, 1988    Suki Lee*    Added new header to denote this as a driver which support the new calls*    PrGetPrinterSpecs and PrGetPgOrientation (and any subsequent new calls). This*    header is 2 words long: first word is 0 followed by a call count word.**    Fixed the jump to an incorrect exit routine in PrPixelmap if unsafe to proceed.*    The correct routine is Exit10, not Exit8.**    The offset table used by font directory search was allocated using the address,*    rather than the contents, of the variable (lda # instead of lda) as the size.** d4* January 3, 1989     Suki Lee*    Added back in font substitution code which got lost when the code was restructured*    for the adding of LaserWriter font query code.** January 4, 1989     Suki Lee*    Modified code to check if font requested is built-in for the LaserWriter being*    used, if so, no search is needed to see if the font is resident in the printer.**    Modified the PostScript procedure 'LW' in prepfile.asm to return 0 for LW, 1*    for LW+ or II and 2 for non-LW.**    Modified status window size and status string placement in dialogdata.asm to*    accommodate the longer status string (due to addition of the job name field).*    Took out CR at the beginning of the status string so the message starts toward*    the top of the box instead of in the middle.** d5* January 19, 1989     Suki Lee*    Added a new input parameter, handle to the print record, to PrGetPgOrientation.** d6* February 1, 1989     Suki Lee*    Added in query comments so printing to spoolers will work once again. Two queries,*    one for printer specs and one for font list, are used. The spooler uses canned*    PostScript code to perform each query. In order to simplify things, the same PostScript*    code is used when printing directly to a printer. Code to read the response and the*    stuffing of the buffer had to be modified accordingly. Removed the "fdir" procedure*    from Prepfile.asm.** February 3, 1989     Suki Lee*    Modified PrValidate so that it will no longer call CiXMetrics if the print record is*    valid for the printer type and is the correct version. This was not necessary and*    caused problems for applications that want to modify fields in the record such as the*    page rectangle.*    Also modified the values for the horizontal resolution from 42 to 40 in 320 mode and*    from 84 to 80 in 640 mode. The incorrect values cause margin sizes to be wrong.** February 10, 1989    Suki Lee*    Converted all file calls from ProDOS to GS/OS class 1. Added ability to create mutiple*    files for PostScript output using Command-F. The files will be named PostScript.GSxx*    where xx is 00-99 numbered sequentially in the order created.**    Bug fix in PrValidate: the print record handle is now dereferenced before using.** d7* February 23, 1989    Suki Lee*    Further bug fix in PrValidate: PtrToHand call is changed to BlockMove since the print*    record handle has been deferenced. An error was being returned from the PtrToHand call,*    causing the code to display the dialogs to be skipped.**    Moved the memory disposal code for the handles used in SetUpNameTables so that disposal*    only happens if the memory has been allocated. The old way could cause screen refresh*    problems if the print job is cancelled at the early part of the job.**    Added GetStatus call in the wait loop of OpenLaser. This enables the status box to*    reflect the status of the LaserWriter even before the connection is established.** d8* March 1, 1989        Suki Lee*    Rev 1 of NTX boards prints garbage if the manualfeed timer is set to anything higher*    than the default 60 seconds. (Printer Testing Group of SQA is investigating the cause*    as of this writing.) Added PostScript code in PrepFile.asm to check the product*    entry of the printer to leave that timer alone if it's an NTX. For all other models,*    the timer is set to wait 5 minutes.** March 7, 1989        Suki Lee*    Modified bitmap font downloading code to use pointers to the various parts of the*    font record on QuickDraw's zero page. This is necessary due to changes in the Font*    Manager - font strike larger than 64K and in QuickDraw - FastFonts.** March 8, 1989        Suki Lee*    Added code in PrValidate to copy the print record into the local data stroage area*    since the driver code works off the local copy of the print record.** March 14,1989        Suki Lee*    Added initialization of two variables: ZeroPage and SCBValue in PrValidate. This is*    a measure to safeguard against cases where the application enters the print loop*    without calling PrDefault, PrStlDialog or PrJobDialog, where these variables are*    currently being initialized.** d9* April 3, 1989        Suki Lee*    Fixed bug in QD verb erase to fill with background pattern or color. Currently, white*    is used to fill. Procedure vrb in Prepfile.asm is modified to just do an eofill.** April 4, 1989        Suki Lee*    Rewrote CheckVerb to be more compact.** April 17, 1989       Suki Lee*    Added flag to indicate error on a status call. If there is such an error, most likely*    the printer is off line or problem with connection, and we exit at that point.**    Added new routine to send foreground color as a solid pattern for text printing. There*    was a bug before where the pen pattern was used for text.**    Added error checking in MakeBMFont's loops which sends data to the printer, in case of*    connection errors to the printer as well as user cancel.** April 18, 1989       Suki Lee*    Modified AddTextToWBuff and AddStrToWBuff to eliminate a 255 character text length limit.*    This effected mainly PicComments. This bug was reported by Claris.** d10* April 21, 1989       Suki Lee*    Fixed bug in RoundRect where the OvalWidth and OvalHeight parameters were swapped. Also*    modified PostScript procedure to use both height and width of the oval to calculate the*    radius of the arc. 640 mode corners look squished due to the 1:2 (x:y) scale factor.*    This bug was reported by Claris.** d11* April 25, 1989       Suki Lee*    Fixed bug in framing of objects where part of the frame was outside the boundary of the*    shape. The shape is now used as a clipping path, and the pen size is doubled, so the*    outer half is clipped and inner half is equal to the pen size requested.  This bug was*    reported by Claris.** d12* April 27, 1989       Suki Lee*    Bug fix: Index to the font name buffer is off by 1 so the lengths were stored on top of*    the last character of the previous name. Also the index to this buffer was not updated*    in the loop which calculates the length and the offset. These conditions caused resident*    fonts to not match with the font being printed. BRC #48609** d13* May 2, 1989          Suki Lee*    Revert PrValidate to recalculating the whole print record each time, so applications can*    modifiy one field and have the rest of the record be consistent. Change code in PrOpenDoc*    to just look at the type and version field of the print record instead of calling*    PrValidate. This is needed for Iduna printing.** d14* May 16, 1989         Suki Lee*    Add additional error checking for status calls so that no other PAP calls will be issued*    if the printer is not responding. Currently, it looks like AppleTalk is stuck in an*    infinite loop if a name look up happens while another is in progress. Tim Harrington is*    investigating if the problem is a bug or as designed. BRC #49183 + 47473 & 47474 revisited.** May 24, 1989	   Suki Lee*    Fixed cut and paste error in PrValidate which caused the style dialog to contain incorrect*    default value when switching from a different printer.** June 5, 1989	   Suki Lee*    Modified constants for Hres and Vres so the page sizes and margins are more accurate. For*    next release, make use of the additional built in predefined sizes in LW+ and LW II.**    Added initialization of variables ZeroPage and SCBValue in PrOpenDoc as well, since some*    apps do not call anything else before the print loop.** June 14, 1989        Suki Lee*    Expanded buffer used by PAPStatus from 128 to 260 bytes, according to errata sheet to*    AppleShare Programmer's Guide to the IIGS. 4 bytes unused + 1 byte length + 255 bytes data.** June 16, 1989        Suki Lee*    Bug fix:*      - If the pattern of color is set to white, then a pixelmap is printed, the internal array*        is set to black. But due to the save/restore around pixelmaps, the currentgray is still*        white, causing any black objects not to be printed. Removed the jsr to setBlack since*        currentgray does not affect images.**      - The procedure to set the screen back to normal after a pat call is incorrect. This causes*        the screen dots to be too large when a pixelmap is printed after a pattern or color change.*        Added currentscreen call in dictionary to set up variables with the initial conditions so*        that we can use them to set the screen back to normal in setBlack. BRC #50891** June 17, 1989        Suki Lee*     Added call to set screen back to default before doing a pixelmap. Should not affect the world*     since it happens inside a save/restore.*** Version 3.1 on system disk 5.0.3** August 16, 1990      Ben Koning*     Brought QD equates that were included from elsewhere into this source file.  This is*     very bad if the QD equates ever change, but makes it much easier to build.  Also does not*     use all.macros file nor the pushptr macro anymore.  This should be changed back.** October 12, 1990     Ben Koning	Desperate bug fixes:*     Wes Johnson found postscript syntax error in error messages for /ep and /vm ps routines:*     the code fragments should end in '= flush' and not '=flush'.  Fixed in prepfile.asm.**     Changed version ID (appears in print record init, dialog boxes, etc) to $0301.  Changed it*     in all places, including where it is set to default with a ds.b (caused bug!).**     PrOpenDoc now calls OpenLaser a second time in trying to open a PAP connection.  Some LW*     models won't communicate at all if a page from the previous job is still ejecting.  This*     can cause problems for those apps which treat each page as a new document.**     The GetStatus routine, called very often before/after reading/writing, had two lines*     commented out without comment or apparent cause.  The two lines have been re-activated.*     These two lines checked a 'allowstatus' flag which would cause it to not execute the*     StatusLaser routine.  The StatusLaser routine always does a papread.  It also does a*     papstatus every 5 seconds.  The papreads were apparently interfering with the reading-in of*     the printer's font list during PrOpenDoc.  It is not clear why these two lines were*     commented out, but in fact it seems safer to have them activated, both to fix this bug,*     and for other GetStatus invocations as well.**     Fixed AddStrToWBuff so that it can now handle (ie, do nothing) on zero-length pstrings.*     NOTE:  What should really be done is that the username be called "Unknown" or something*     to that effect, either here locally in the LW driver, or, better yet, in other code such*     as the print manager or the print network CDEVs or elsewhere.** August 27, 1991	   Ben Koning	Bug fixes for system disk 6.0:*     Fixed job and style dialog not updating (ie, with video keyboard) problem.**     Incremented version number to $0302 (3.2).**     In job dialog, Command-M toggles manual/auto feed.**     In job and style dialog, ESC is now a key equivalent for Cancel.**     Command-period abort key hit right after job dialog OK caused hang.  Fixed by checking if*     iPrErr is nonzero just before ReadLaser calls (the ReadLaser call went into an infinite loop*     if there was an error because the command that was supposed to be sent might not have*     completely sent and thus no response will ever happen from the device.**     Some (but not all) special extended hi-ascii characters don't work: not fixing this.**     In job and style dialog, Cancel key equivalent now hilites correctly and Command-Period is*     works in addition to ESC.******************************************************************************************************** BEGIN 6.0.1** July 3..4, 1992	    Matt Deatherage*     Changed PostScript definition of /spf (the spotting function) to get it*     defined correctly on level 2 printers, using a hard-coded default spot*     function for when the dictionary isn't of HalfToneType 1.**     Incremented version number to $0303 (3.3).  Changed copyright to include 1992.**     Changed drawing of job dialog to include a call to PrGetNetworkName so we*     can draw the chosen printer's name in the job dialog.  If there is no*     network printer (PrGetNetworkName returns NIL), we draw "No network - not*     supported".  Either Dave or I will change this to DrawStringWidth soon and*     relayout the job dialog because it just doesn't fit well. (Search 7/3/92)**     When we bypass the code that sets up the name tables and sends queries to the*     printer (because we're creating a PS file), we now explictly set the LWType*     variable to 1, indicating a LaserWriter Plus or II.  Now the code can find*     all the standard 35N fonts in the built-in name tables, instead of just the*     four faces used in LaserWriters plus Sonata, Carta and Shaston.  This means*     you can now dump PS files that work correctly with styled variants of the*     35N fonts.** July 9, 1992	Dave Lyons*     Changed the printer-name-in-job-dialog thing to use DrawStringWidth when*     running under 6.0.1 or later (it uses DrawString in 6.0 and earlier, in case*     we want to tell people they can use this driver under old systems).**     Cleaned up a lot of stray semicolons & stuff.  Normalized DEA to DEC A,*     INA to INC A.  Fixed capitalization of tool call macros.  Optimized pushing*     result space in some places (PHA PHA instead of PushLong #0).** November 13, 1992	    Matt Deatherage*     Oops -- making level 2 color printing work broke level 1 color printing.*     The test to see if currentscreen returns a function destroys the function*     on the stack.  Now we 'dup' it first so it's still there after the 'eq.'*     Adds four more bytes, big deal.** 18-Feb-93	Dave Lyons*     Changed AddStrToWBuff so a NIL pointer doesn't add anything to the output.*     This way we don't get a garbage username in the file when PMGetUsername*     returns NIL because we have no network connection (see also October 12,*     1990 for related fix).** 25-Mar-93	Dave Lyons** Added 3 lines in CkPrinterStatus to nuke an infinite loop.  If our session* timed out we start getting error $0806 from ReadLaser, but we didn't care.******************************************************************************************************** THINGS TO DO** Easy things:*   Change many PushWord #0 and PushLong #0 to PHAs or LDA/PHAs.*   Change lots of NewDItem calls to be table based*   Make a subroutine for FindHandle+DisposeHandle sequence (pass pointer in XA)** Hard things:*   Print with better fonts (higher quality bitmaps and/or hook for other kinds of fonts)******************************************************************************************************	include 'm16.util2'	include 'm16.misctool'	include 'm16.memory'	include 'm16.event'	include 'm16.quickdraw'	include 'm16.qdaux'	include 'm16.font'	include 'm16.intmath'	include 'm16.window'	include 'm16.dialog'	include 'm16.lineedit'	include 'm16.control'	include 'm16.print'	include 'm16.loader'	include 'm16.gsos'	include 'special.macros'	include 'e16.dialog'	include 'e16.QuickDraw'	blanks off	string asisUS	equ 0FR	equ 1Pays	equ USVersionNb	equ $0303	; Version 3.2VersionMaj	equ $03	; Version 3.XVersionMin	equ $03	; Vertion X.2;----------------------------------------------;; Important equates;TRUE           	equ $FFFFFALSE         	equ $0000EOFError	equ $004C	; GS/OS errorDupPathName	equ $0047	; GS/OS errorNameNotFound	equ $0805	; AppleTalk errorSessionClosed	equ $0806	; AppleTalk er